00:42:53,676 --> 00:42:55,047
SIG-003 · 2.

750
00:42:55,047 --> 00:42:58,705
"Wrong place": measuring the DOM in an effect

751
00:42:59,830 --> 00:43:03,481
effect() is for synchronising state with something outside Angular's templates.

752
00:43:03,481 --> 00:43:07,864
It is not timed to the DOM: it runs during change detection,

753
00:43:07,864 --> 00:43:12,246
so the measurement can happen against a layout that is not final.

754
00:43:12,246 --> 00:43:16,263
Reading layout (getBoundingClientRect) and then writing styles in the same callback,

755
00:43:16,263 --> 00:43:20,280
for many popovers, also forces the browser to recalculate layout repeatedly.

756
00:43:21,656 --> 00:43:23,110
SIG-003 · 2.

757
00:43:23,110 --> 00:43:26,989
"Wrong place": measuring the DOM in an effect

758
00:43:28,114 --> 00:43:28,897
Fix: afterRenderEffect.

759
00:43:28,897 --> 00:43:33,982
It runs after Angular has updated the DOM, splits work into phases (earlyRead,

760
00:43:33,982 --> 00:43:38,676
write, mixedReadWrite, read) so reads and writes from many components are batched,

761
00:43:38,676 --> 00:43:43,760
and never runs during server-side rendering, where there is no layout to measure.

762
00:43:45,136 --> 00:43:48,465
SIG-003 · Answer · code 1/4

763
00:43:49,590 --> 00:43:55,001
The correction pairs registration with cleanup and separates geometry reads from coordinate writes.

764
